{
 "note": "Eight original leaders for the Arena and the Mat, cleaned from the Landing showdown sheets. Each atlas is a 4x4 grid of 96x128 native cells in pose order; cells[i] is pose i's opaque bounds [x, y, w, h] and anchors[i] its foot point [x, y] (the ground line under the feet), both in native atlas px; the grid cell itself is [i % 4 * 96, floor(i / 4) * 128, 96, 128]. Draw a pose so its anchor lands on the world foot point; the @3x atlas is the same pixels at 3x (multiply every number by 3). Both are indexed PNGs: index 0 is clear, every other pixel is opaque and one of the trainer's palette colours. sourceCrops[i] is the same pose in the Landing sheet in the Landing crop convention [x, y, w, h, footX, groundY] (1 px padding, groundY = lowest row + 1), with the true foot. Rear poses 12 to 15 face upper right; never mirror a front pose.",
